# Anything that a Linux box or a shell has to parse must check out with LF,
# regardless of the platform it was edited on. A CRLF line ending here is not a
# cosmetic diff: `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` is a shebang for an interpreter that
# doesn't exist, and systemd reads the trailing \r as part of the value — so a
# unit's ExecStart silently points at a path with a carriage return in it.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
env.example text eol=lf
